# SCOPE 4  |  Tier 2 saddle points: B3LYP-D3(BJ)/def2-TZVP, OptTS + FREQ
# State: V-TS3 final Al-O cleavage saddle  |  register row: V-TS3-T2-V06
# Start: TIER 1 candidate optts3_bandC_ci (1 imaginary mode, -40.33 cm-1; barrier
#      bracketed 483.80 - 488.54 kJ/mol vs V-I2).
# Why: least urgent of the three saddles - the barrier is so large that the qualitative
#      conclusion (the third cleavage is prohibitive) survives without it. Run last.
# Watch: a -40 cm-1 imaginary mode is close to flat-mode noise. If it grows or the
#      count changes at Tier 2, treat the saddle as not established.
# Cost warning: OptTS with an exact initial Hessian (%geom Calc_Hess true) on 30
#      atoms is the most expensive job class in this package; treat 10-60 h per job
#      as the honest bracket and run them one at a time with a budget stop.
# Gate: TERMINATED NORMALLY + converged + exactly 1 imaginary mode animating the
#      reacting bond; then the A4 displacement test.

! B3LYP D3BJ def2-TZVP RIJCOSX def2/J TightSCF DefGrid3 OptTS Freq

%pal nprocs 4 end
%maxcore 3000

%scf
  MaxIter 300
end

%geom
  Calc_Hess true
  MaxIter 200
end

%freq
  Temp 298.15, 1003.15
end

* xyzfile 0 1 xyz/v-ts3.xyz
